      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Based on [[credential-scoping]], here\u0027s how the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment:\n\n**The key mechanism**: the Hub never loads the API key into its own process at all. Instead:\n\n1. A **local secrets loader** reads the Anthropic API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup.\n2. It **injects the key directly into the environment** of the spawned child process (the Ingest agent) immediately before that process starts.\n3. The **Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated** \u2014 the key never exists there.\n\nThis design ensures that even if the Hub process is compromised or behaves unexpectedly, it cannot leak the credential simply by examining its own environment variables. The key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually needs it to call the Anthropic API.\n\nThe Query agent uses the same model: it also receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn time, never inherited from or stored in the Hub\u0027s process environment.",
